_test_outputs/
_generated/

# Reference materials — copyrighted PDFs etc. kept locally only
עותק של Sketchy.pdf
*.pdf
# ...but our own generated study materials are original content — keep them
!schedule/question_booklet.pdf

# The owner's recorded academic lectures: 28 files, 14GB, served from GCS
# (see scripts/upload_lectures.py). Never belongs in git.
הקלטות לימודי המשך/
# Prototype scratch output (renders, composites)
_proto/
_view/
_venue_input.json

# The venue drafts are real deliverables, not scratch — many hours of
# authoring and review live in them, and they were only ever on one machine.
# _venue_audit.json stays ignored: it is derived, rebuilt by _venue_audit.py.
_venue_audit.json
_feed/
_bulk/ft/

# Archived run bundles — big media, already on the releases
_bulk/day-*/
_bulk/audio/
_bulk/infographics/

# QC: textbook text and per-call work files never go in git.
#
# Inverted on purpose. Spec §5.10 commits exactly five things by explicit path
# and everything else under _qc/ is either the books' own text or per-call
# scratch: _qc/cache/ is the reflowed text of six copyrighted textbooks,
# _qc/src/ and _qc/work/ hold the bundles built out of them, _qc/<tag>/
# judgments/ stores the judge's answer as it arrived — and §5.8's schema makes
# every coverage row carry "source_quote: <verbatim from that page>", one per
# unit, ~40-60 units a chapter, three calls a chapter, 68 chapters —
# and _qc/<tag>/lint.json names the book and page of every unsourced value.
# Listing those by hand is how the first three came to be covered and the rest
# did not; a tree worked with `git add -A` and 60+ untracked files only has to
# lose that race once, and a commit of the books' text cannot be taken back.
# So: ignore _qc/ wholesale, then re-admit §5.10's list and nothing else.
# _qc/<tag>/journal.json is deliberately NOT re-admitted — it is not on §5.10's
# list, it holds no book text, and it is rebuilt by the next run.
_qc/*
!_qc/REPORT.md
!_qc/state.json
# the per-chapter directories, so git descends into them at all…
!_qc/*/
# …but inside one, only the verdict and the fixes it applied
_qc/*/*
!_qc/*/verdict.json
!_qc/*/fixes.json
# the pristine release bytes, whole: this is what qc_revert rebuilds from and
# what §2.5 ("never lose an asset") is about
!_qc/orig/**

# Printed→PDF page maps of the books (§5.10, "any pages.json")
**/pages.json
